{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "crash-anchor-eligibility-base-rate-census",
    "parent": null,
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Base rate of crash victims already holding undelivered outbound sends, before any anchored-crash mechanism is built",
    "description": "Read-only instrumentation in spur/spur-core/src/simulator/: at every fault-injection decision point increment counters in util_stats.rs for crash_census.decisions, crash_census.victim_had_inflight_sends, crash_census.any_candidate_had_inflight_sends, and a bucketed histogram crash_census.inflight_bucket_{0,1,2,3plus} over the chosen victim's undelivered outbound count. Values are read from the in-flight send bookkeeping already maintained for the h1 hazard; no new field in exec.rs/state.rs/path.rs. Gated by the existing `stats` flag plus new `emit_crash_census` (bool, default false), serialized through the deliveryEffects block. Diff must be counter-only.",
    "category": "feedback",
    "buildsOn": [
      "crash_recovery / post_fault_ops",
      "util_stats",
      "counters-piggyback-serialized-block"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "The crash-anchoring family has four closed attempts and zero merges (send-anchored-crash-points, delayed-send-anchored-crash, recovery-anchored-to-own-inflight-sends at -0.0625, coverage-guided-fault-placement at 0.0000) and none of them measured the gating predicate's base rate first. If victims already hold in-flight sends in most decisions, every anchored-crash variant degenerates into the uniform selector and the family should be closed outright rather than retried a fifth time; if the rate is low, there is a real multiplier at the site the relaxation-gap ablation names. This is the cheapest way to license or kill the family, and it is a strict precondition on the sibling mechanism below.",
    "generalityArgument": "Counts fault-injection decisions and per-node undelivered outbound message counts, both simulator-level; no protocol identifier appears in the diff.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-30T11:40:00.000Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "Red team: another zero-risk counter hypothesis in a pool already dominated by them, and its answer may be 'the predicate is near-universal', which yields no ladder movement at all. Accepted only as a gate: it must run before crash-timing-anchored-to-outbound-send-burst, and if victim_had_inflight_sends/decisions > 0.8 the anchored-crash family is closed as a block rather than re-proposed. Falsifier: counters populate and the ratio exceeds 0.8 -> anchoring is vacuous; ratio below ~0.4 with a non-degenerate inflight_bucket histogram -> the mechanism has a stated multiplier. Any counter identically zero means the fault-decision site was mis-located and nothing is concluded. Scaffolding label; not merge credit."
  },
